      "end": 815,
      "end_line": 18,
      "line": 18,
      "start": 534
    },
    "text": "Claude Code and `agy` let the user attach commands to events. Delphi's enforcement lives in the daemon, and a command that could return \"allow\" would be a way around it. So Delphi offers hooks that **cannot loosen anything**: commands that watch, and commands that can only say no."
  }
